1
00:00:04,702 --> 00:00:13,032
Run a telehealth visit — Clinical ▸ Telehealth — Create a virtual visit from an appointment, attach a consent form, and join it.

2
00:00:18,509 --> 00:00:25,840
Clinical ▸ Telehealth. The green banner names the connected platform — here, Google Meet.

3
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:35,142
Your administrator connects that account once. Clinicians never touch credentials.

4
00:00:35,142 --> 00:00:46,662
A session is built from a booked appointment, so the patient, provider and time are already right.

5
00:00:46,662 --> 00:00:58,065
Attach a consent form and it arrives in the patient’s portal before the call, not during it.

6
00:00:58,065 --> 00:01:08,120
AureonCare confirms what it is about to do, then creates the meeting.

7
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:19,488
The visit now sits under Upcoming Sessions, tagged with the platform and carrying its join link.

8
00:01:19,488 --> 00:01:29,312
Joining marks the session in progress, so the rest of the team can see you are in it.

9
00:01:29,312 --> 00:01:33,700
The meeting room opens in a new tab: https://meet.google.com/rzn-hbfa-uwc

10
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:41,268
Need a call right now with no booking behind it? Instant creates a room immediately — use it for the unplanned.

11
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:56,369
What you just did

12
00:01:57,006 --> 00:02:06,006
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
